        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString.__str__>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString._key>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString.n3> ;
    slkg:lineEnd 66 ;
    slkg:lineStart 26 ;
    slkg:qualifiedName "starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString" .

<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/class/starlayergraph.model.triple.TripleTerm> a slkg:Class ;
    rdfs:label "TripleTerm" ;
    rdfs:comment """An RDF 1.2 triple term — a triple used as a resource.

Value-typed: two instances with the same (s, p, o) are equal and have the
same hash. A plain Python 3-tuple is coerced to TripleTerm wherever the
StarLayerGraph API expects a node.

_namespace_manager is set by StarLayerGraph._restore() when returning a
TripleTerm from a query result so that __str__ can emit prefixed names.
It is excluded from equality and hashing.""" ;
    slkg:commentText "Slots that may only be written once (during __init__)" ;
    slkg:hasMethod <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.triple.TripleTerm.__eq__>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.triple.TripleTerm.__hash__>,
