<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.serializers.jsonld12.serialize_jsonld12> a slkg:Function ;
    rdfs:label "serialize_jsonld12" ;
    rdfs:comment """Serialize a StarLayerGraph to JSON-LD 1.2 text.

Triple terms are emitted as top-level nodes with ``@type: rdf:TripleTerm``
and ``rdf:subject / rdf:predicate / rdf:object`` properties, compacted
the same way every other key/value in the document is. ``@context``
always carries ``tt:``/``rdf:`` (intrinsic to the encoding) plus whatever
other namespaces this graph has bound *and* actually uses - so e.g. a
graph with ``g.bind("ex", ...)`` gets ``ex:alice`` in the output instead
of a raw ``http://example.org/alice``, the same compaction every other
StarLayer format (turtle12, trig12, ...) already gives you.""" ;
    slkg:commentText "1. Emit a top-level rdf:TripleTerm node for every registered TripleTerm.",
        "2. Emit regular (user-visible) triples.",
        "3. Assemble output — TripleTerm nodes first, then subject nodes.",
        "@id-string -> JSON-LD node object" ;
    slkg:hasParameter <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Ffunction%2Fstarlayergraph.serializers.jsonld12.serialize_jsonld12%3A%3Ag%3A%3A0> ;
    slkg:lineEnd 236 ;
    slkg:lineStart 191 ;
    slkg:qualifiedName "starlayergraph.serializers.jsonld12.serialize_jsonld12" ;
    slkg:signature "def serialize_jsonld12(g) -> str" .

