<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starshacl.engine.normalization.normalize_to_starlayer_graph> a slkg:Function ;
    rdfs:label "normalize_to_starlayer_graph" ;
    rdfs:comment """Normalize input graph to StarLayerGraph.

A plain rdflib.Graph is always converted. Existing StarLayerGraph instances
are returned as-is.

``force_default_union``: when ``value`` is an ``rdflib.Dataset`` (or
``StarLayerDataset``, a subclass), setting this mutates ``value.default_union
= True`` before conversion - matching pySHACL's own native behavior when
given a raw ``Dataset`` directly as ``ont_graph`` (``pyshacl/validator.py``:
``if isinstance(self.ont_graph, rdflib.Dataset): self.ont_graph.default_union
= True``), so ontology triples across all named graphs are visible for
inference regardless of how the caller constructed the dataset. Not used
for ``data_graph``/``shacl_graph`` - pySHACL doesn't auto-union those
either, only ``ont_graph``.""" ;
    slkg:hasParameter <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Ffunction%2Fstarshacl.engine.normalization.normalize_to_starlayer_graph%3A%3Aforce_default_union%3A%3A2>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Ffunction%2Fstarshacl.engine.normalization.normalize_to_starlayer_graph%3A%3Aname%3A%3A1>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Ffunction%2Fstarshacl.engine.normalization.normalize_to_starlayer_graph%3A%3Avalue%3A%3A0> ;
    slkg:lineEnd 41 ;
    slkg:lineStart 8 ;
    slkg:qualifiedName "starshacl.engine.normalization.normalize_to_starlayer_graph" ;
    slkg:signature "def normalize_to_starlayer_graph(value: Any, *, name: str, force_default_union: bool) -> Any" .

<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starshacl.meta_shapes._load_pyshacl_base_meta_shapes> a slkg:Function ;
    rdfs:label "_load_pyshacl_base_meta_shapes" ;
    rdfs:comment """A fresh, independent copy of pySHACL's own bundled SHACL-of-SHACL
meta-shapes graph, loaded directly from its ``shacl-shacl.ttl`` asset
(not the pickle pySHACL's own ``meta_shacl`` mechanism uses, avoiding
any dependence on pickle-format compatibility across pySHACL versions;
not pySHACL's own process-wide cached graph object either, so nothing
here ever mutates what a caller using plain ``pyshacl.validate(...,
meta_shacl=True)`` directly would see).""" ;
    slkg:lineEnd 105 ;
    slkg:lineStart 90 ;
    slkg:qualifiedName "starshacl.meta_shapes._load_pyshacl_base_meta_shapes" ;
    slkg:signature "def _load_pyshacl_base_meta_shapes() -> Graph" .

<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starshacl.meta_shapes._remove_blank_node_subtree> a slkg:Function ;
    rdfs:label "_remove_blank_node_subtree" ;
    rdfs:comment """Remove ``node``'s own triples, and (recursively) the triples of any
blank node it points to - so excising a property-shape blank node also
removes structure hanging off it (e.g. ``sh:in``'s list), not just the
blank node's own top-level triples, leaving no orphaned garbage behind.""" ;
    slkg:hasParameter <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Ffunction%2Fstarshacl.meta_shapes._remove_blank_node_subtree%3A%3A_seen%3A%3A2>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Ffunction%2Fstarshacl.meta_shapes._remove_blank_node_subtree%3A%3Agraph%3A%3A0>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Ffunction%2Fstarshacl.meta_shapes._remove_blank_node_subtree%3A%3Anode%3A%3A1> ;
    slkg:lineEnd 87 ;
