    slkg:lineEnd 173 ;
    slkg:lineStart 158 ;
    slkg:qualifiedName "starsparql.from_rdf.rdf_to_collection" ;
    slkg:signature "def rdf_to_collection(graph: Graph, root) -> list[Query]" .

<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf.rdf_to_query> a slkg:Function ;
    rdfs:label "rdf_to_query" ;
    rdfs:comment """Decode ``root`` (as produced by ``to_rdf.query_to_rdf``) back into an
rdflib ``Query`` — same type ``prepareQuery``/``translateQuery`` return.

The returned ``Query``'s ``Prologue`` is reconstructed from
``salg:base``/``salg:prologuePrefix`` on ``root`` (see vocab.py's
"Prologue (BASE/PREFIX)" section) — this fixes real evaluation-time
behavior (``BASE``-relative ``IRI()``/``URI()`` builtin resolution), but
does *not* make ``algebra.translateAlgebra`` emit prefixed names: that
function never reads ``query.prologue`` at all, confirmed empirically,
so its output stays full-IRI-only regardless.""" ;
    slkg:commentText "Recompute the _vars/lazy bookkeeping to_rdf.py deliberately doesn't",
        "decoded tree is evaluator-ready exactly like one built straight from",
        "encode (see _INTERNAL_BOOKKEEPING_KEYS there) — the same two passes",
        "query text.",
        "translateQuery() itself runs on a freshly-built algebra tree, so the" ;
    slkg:hasParameter <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Ffunction%2Fstarsparql.from_rdf.rdf_to_query%3A%3Agraph%3A%3A0>,
