<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.graph.starlayer_dataset.StarLayerDataset.parse> a slkg:Method ;
    rdfs:label "parse" ;
    rdfs:comment """Parse RDF data into named-graph contexts.

format='turtle12' — Turtle 1.2; triples go into the default graph as a StarLayerGraph.
format='trig12'   — TriG 1.2; each GRAPH block becomes a StarLayerGraph.
                    Plain Turtle content (no GRAPH blocks) goes into the default graph.
format='nq12'     — N-Quads 1.2; each distinct graph name becomes a StarLayerGraph.
format='trix12'   — TriX 1.2 XML; each <graph> block becomes a StarLayerGraph.
All other formats delegate to rdflib (no triple-term support).""" ;
    slkg:commentText "StarLayerGraph.parse()'s trig12 branch) - decode back",
        "into real TripleTerm objects before sg.add() so a",
        "native-backend context gets its real <<( )>> encoding",
        "parse_trig12_named() returns the rdf-1.1 backend's own",
        "so routing turtle12 through the trig12 path is correct and safe.",
        "tt:HASH encoding (same as parse_trig12(), see",
        "turtle12 is Turtle-only (no GRAPH blocks); trig12 is a strict superset,",
        "via _native_add(), not the flat encoding fragments." ;
    slkg:hasParameter <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarlayergraph.graph.starlayer_dataset.StarLayerDataset.parse%3A%3Adata%3A%3A6>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarlayergraph.graph.starlayer_dataset.StarLayerDataset.parse%3A%3Afile%3A%3A5>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarlayergraph.graph.starlayer_dataset.StarLayerDataset.parse%3A%3Aformat%3A%3A3>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarlayergraph.graph.starlayer_dataset.StarLayerDataset.parse%3A%3Akwargs%3A%3A7>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarlayergraph.graph.starlayer_dataset.StarLayerDataset.parse%3A%3Alocation%3A%3A4>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarlayergraph.graph.starlayer_dataset.StarLayerDataset.parse%3A%3ApublicID%3A%3A2>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarlayergraph.graph.starlayer_dataset.StarLayerDataset.parse%3A%3Aself%3A%3A0>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarlayergraph.graph.starlayer_dataset.StarLayerDataset.parse%3A%3Asource%3A%3A1> ;
    slkg:lineEnd 370 ;
    slkg:lineStart 280 ;
    slkg:qualifiedName "starlayergraph.graph.starlayer_dataset.StarLayerDataset.parse" ;
    slkg:signature "def parse(self, source, publicID, format, location, file, data, **kwargs) -> StarLayerDataset" .

<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.graph.starlayer_dataset.StarLayerDataset.quads> a slkg:Method ;
