<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.graph.starlayer_graph.StarLayerGraph.from_rdflib> a slkg:Method ;
    rdfs:label "from_rdflib" ;
    rdfs:comment """Wrap a plain rdflib.Graph (e.g., from StarLayerTurtleParser).

Namespace bindings, triples, and the TripleTerm registry are all
copied from the source graph.  If the source uses the intermediate
BNode TT encoding (with sl:TripleTerm type markers), it is converted
to content-addressed tt: URIRefs before copying.

source_graph may also be a Dataset/ConjunctiveGraph: triples are read
via its own ``.triples((None, None, None))``, which - like iterating
the dataset directly - honors whatever ``default_union`` it was
constructed with (rdflib default: False), so only its default graph
is copied unless the caller explicitly opted into a unioned view.
Named graphs are never selected implicitly; use
``dataset.get_context(identifier)`` first for a specific one.""" ;
    slkg:hasParameter <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarlayergraph.graph.starlayer_graph.StarLayerGraph.from_rdflib%3A%3Acls%3A%3A0>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarlayergraph.graph.starlayer_graph.StarLayerGraph.from_rdflib%3A%3Asource_graph%3A%3A1> ;
    slkg:lineEnd 1656 ;
    slkg:lineStart 1632 ;
    slkg:qualifiedName "starlayergraph.graph.starlayer_graph.StarLayerGraph.from_rdflib" ;
    slkg:signature "def from_rdflib(cls, source_graph)" .

