<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starshacl.validator.StarShaclValidator._humanize_report_text> a slkg:Method ;
    rdfs:label "_humanize_report_text" ;
    rdfs:comment """Replace encoded triple-term URIs embedded in pySHACL's report text
with a readable ``<<( s p o )>>`` rendering.

pySHACL builds this text per-result before starShacl ever sees it, so
unlike ``report_graph`` (which we decode via ``adapter.decode_graph``)
there's no structured graph to decode - only string substitution
against the adapter's own encoding registry. Applied repeatedly so
nested triple terms (whose components are themselves encoded URIs)
resolve fully.""" ;
    slkg:hasParameter <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarshacl.validator.StarShaclValidator._humanize_report_text%3A%3Areport_text%3A%3A1>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarshacl.validator.StarShaclValidator._humanize_report_text%3A%3Aself%3A%3A0> ;
    slkg:lineEnd 763 ;
    slkg:lineStart 734 ;
    slkg:qualifiedName "starshacl.validator.StarShaclValidator._humanize_report_text" ;
    slkg:signature "def _humanize_report_text(self, report_text: str) -> str" .

<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starshacl.validator.StarShaclValidator._nodes_conforming_to> a slkg:Method ;
    rdfs:label "_nodes_conforming_to" ;
    rdfs:comment """Every non-literal node in ``data_graph`` that conforms to
``where_shape``, for ``sh:targetWhere``. Runs one batched nested
``validate()`` call (candidates as ``sh:targetNode`` on ``where_shape``)
rather than one call per candidate. Excludes the triggering
``(shape_node, sh:targetWhere, where_shape)`` triple from the copy
used for that nested call, or it would re-trigger this exact check on
itself forever.""" ;
    slkg:commentText "\"any sh:focusNode object\" scan wrongly counts as a violation",
        "Only genuine top-level results (reachable from the report node's",
        "against an unrelated candidate.",
        "document) - pySHACL's own report-graph cloning copies that",
        "fails one of where_shape's constraints can have some *other*,",
        "if that value node happens to itself carry a pre-existing",
        "incidental triple along with the value node, which a blanket",
        "ordinary data here, since sht:dataGraph <> loads the whole",
        "own sh:result) count as \"violating\" - not every sh:focusNode",
        "self-describing mf:result expected-validation-report block is",
        "sh:focusNode triple as part of its own data content (confirmed via",
        "the W3C SHACL 1.2 test suite's targetWhere-001 fixture, whose",
        "triple anywhere in the (decoded) report graph. A candidate that",
        "unrelated data-graph node reported as that violation's sh:value;" ;
    slkg:hasParameter <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarshacl.validator.StarShaclValidator._nodes_conforming_to%3A%3Adata_graph%3A%3A1>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarshacl.validator.StarShaclValidator._nodes_conforming_to%3A%3Aself%3A%3A0>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarshacl.validator.StarShaclValidator._nodes_conforming_to%3A%3Ashacl_graph%3A%3A2>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarshacl.validator.StarShaclValidator._nodes_conforming_to%3A%3Ashape_node%3A%3A3>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/parameter/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fhidden-graph%2Fstarlayer%2Fkg%2Fresource%2Fmethod%2Fstarshacl.validator.StarShaclValidator._nodes_conforming_to%3A%3Awhere_shape%3A%3A4> ;
    slkg:lineEnd 551 ;
    slkg:lineStart 496 ;
    slkg:qualifiedName "starshacl.validator.StarShaclValidator._nodes_conforming_to" ;
    slkg:signature "def _nodes_conforming_to(self, data_graph: Any, shacl_graph: Any, shape_node: Any, where_shape: Any) -> list[Any]" .

