<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/module/starsparql.from_rdf> a slkg:Module ;
    rdfs:label "starsparql.from_rdf" ;
    dcterms:identifier "starsparql.from_rdf" ;
    rdfs:comment """Decode RDF triples (as produced by ``to_rdf.py``) back into an rdflib
SPARQL algebra tree / ``Query`` object — runnable directly via
``rdflib.plugins.sparql.evaluate.evalQuery`` or serializable back to query
text via ``rdflib.plugins.sparql.algebra.translateAlgebra``.

The hard part decoding has that encoding doesn't: rdflib's evaluator
requires *expression* nodes (``RelationalExpression``, ``Builtin_BOUND``,
``Function``, ...) to be actual ``Expr`` instances with a bound ``_evalfn``
(``rdflib.plugins.sparql.parserutils.value()`` raises on a plain
``CompValue`` used as an expression — "What do I do with this CompValue?").
That binding happens once, at *parse* time, via each grammar production's
``Comp(name, ...).setEvalFn(fn)`` call in ``rdflib.plugins.sparql.parser``.
Rather than hand-transcribing that table (name -> evalfn) — which would
silently drift out of sync with whatever rdflib version is actually
installed — ``_discover_expr_evalfns()`` below rebuilds it by walking the
live pyparsing grammar object graph in that module and collecting every
``Comp`` with a bound ``evalfn``. Same generic-mirror principle as the
encoder in ``to_rdf.py`` and the design note in ``vocab.py``.""" ;
    slkg:belongsToPackage <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/package/starsparql> ;
    slkg:commentText "(no exception) while silently never binding `?z`. Confirmed via a real",
        "(node name, key) pairs whose value must decode to a genuine Python",
        "Reserved key names _encode_prologue (to_rdf.py) writes directly onto a",
        "Scoped by node name, not key name alone: `start`/`length` are also",
        "StarLayerGraph reproduction comparing results against plain rdflib.",
        "`Builtin_SUBSTR`'s own parameter names (SPARQL's `SUBSTR(str, start[,",
        "`Literal`s — `operators.Builtin_SUBSTR` calls `numeric(expr.start)`,",
        "`if` regardless of its actual value, since it's a non-empty string either",
        "`start`/`length` to plain ints too, and `evalExtend` silently swallows",
        "here.",
        "instance. A bare key-name match previously converted `Builtin_SUBSTR`'s",
        "int/bool, not merely an rdflib Literal that happens to compare equal to",
        "length])`), a completely unrelated node where they must stay real",
        "mechanism documented throughout this project's own findings) rather than",
        "one — Slice.start/.length are passed straight to itertools.islice, which",
        "query/update root node — see _decode_comp_value's use of this below.",
        "raising - so a decoded `BIND(SUBSTR(...) AS ?z)` looked like it worked",
        "requires a real int; a boolean Literal is always truthy in a plain Python",
        "that error into \"leave the BIND target unbound\" (same swallowing",
        "way. See vocab.py's \"Bare Python strings\" section for the str case, which",
        "which raises `SPARQLTypeError` for anything that isn't a `Literal`",
        "— unlike int/bool — is handled generically rather than by listing keys" ;
    slkg:contains <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._comp_value_type>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_binding_row>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_comp_value>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_list>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_path>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_prologue>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_quads_map>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_triple_pattern>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._discover_expr_evalfns>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._to_python_deep>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf.rdf_to_collection>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf.rdf_to_query>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf.rdf_to_update> ;
    slkg:defines <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._comp_value_type>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_binding_row>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_comp_value>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_list>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_path>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_prologue>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_quads_map>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._decode_triple_pattern>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._discover_expr_evalfns>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf._to_python_deep>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf.rdf_to_collection>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf.rdf_to_query>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starsparql.from_rdf.rdf_to_update> ;
    slkg:filePath "packages/sparql/starsparql/from_rdf.py" ;
    slkg:importsModule <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/__future__>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/collections>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/pyparsing>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/rdflib>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/rdflib.collection>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/rdflib.namespace>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/rdflib.paths>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/rdflib.plugins.sparql.algebra>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/rdflib.plugins.sparql.operators>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/rdflib.plugins.sparql.parser>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/rdflib.plugins.sparql.parserutils>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/rdflib.plugins.sparql.sparql>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/module/starsparql.triple_term>,
