<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/module/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring> a slkg:Module ;
    rdfs:label "starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring" ;
    dcterms:identifier "starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring" ;
    rdfs:comment """starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring

Core RDF 1.2 type: DirLangString — a language-tagged string literal carrying
an explicit base text direction ('ltr' or 'rtl'), per rdf:dirLangString
(RDF 1.2 Concepts sec 3.4). Lexical form: "text"@lang--dir.

Encoding follows the same "invisible to public APIs" approach as TripleTerm:
rdflib.Literal(text, lang="en--rtl") raises (rdflib has no notion of the
--dir suffix), so a DirLangString is stored as a plain Literal whose datatype
URI packs (language, direction) - see encode_dirlang_datatype in
starlayergraph.model.encoding. StarLayerGraph encodes/decodes at its read/write
boundary so callers only ever see DirLangString or plain rdflib terms.""" ;
    slkg:belongsToPackage <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/package/starlayergraph> ;
    slkg:contains <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/class/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.decode_dirlangstring>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.encode_dirlangstring>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString.__eq__>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString.__hash__>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString.__init__>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString.__repr__>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString.__setattr__>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString.__str__>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString._key>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/method/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString.n3> ;
    slkg:defines <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/class/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.DirLangString>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.decode_dirlangstring>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring.encode_dirlangstring> ;
    slkg:filePath "packages/graph/starlayergraph/model/dirlangstring.py" ;
    slkg:importsModule <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/external/rdflib>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/module/starlayergraph.model.encoding> ;
    slkg:moduleName "starlayergraph.model.dirlangstring" .

<https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/module/starlayergraph.model.encoding> a slkg:Module ;
    rdfs:label "starlayergraph.model.encoding" ;
    dcterms:identifier "starlayergraph.model.encoding" ;
    rdfs:comment """starlayergraph.model.encoding

Shared constants and hash function for the starlayergraph internal graph encoding.

Triple terms    → content-addressed URIRefs under TT_NS (same content = same URI)
Anon reifiers   → sequential URIRefs under RR_NS (each {| |} block is distinct)
DirLangString   → a Literal whose datatype URI under DIRLANG_NS packs the real
                  language tag and base direction (see decode_dirlang_datatype)""" ;
    slkg:belongsToPackage <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/package/starlayergraph> ;
    slkg:commentText "(s, p, o) always hashes to the same URI everywhere, and a graph that has",
        "<<( )>> queries would otherwise grow this dict forever. Capped size with",
        "Bounded LRU rather than a plain dict, though: correctness of *what a hash",
        "Predicates used in the internal TripleTerm URIRef encoding - shared by",
        "Process-wide memo: tt:HASH URIRef -> (s, p, o) components, populated by the",
        "Sharing this across every graph and query in the process is correct, not a",
        "StarLayerGraph and StarLayerDataset's _is_encoding_triple() checks and by",
        "StarLayerGraph._restore() falls back to this memo to still reconstruct a",
        "again\" for bounded memory - re-computation is just re-running the pure",
        "anonymous reifier URIs",
        "as a plain expression (SELECT projection, BIND, FILTER) rather than a",
        "costs. A long-running process issuing many distinct ground TRIPLE()/",
        "dirLangString datatype encoding",
        "given hash \"means\" doesn't depend on which graph is asking - the same",
        "graph-pattern term - a value that, like a literal IRI, is constructed on",
        "hash function, so eviction has no correctness cost, only a cache-miss cost.",
        "leak: tt_hash is a pure, deterministic function of (s, p, o), so what a",
        "means* doesn't bound how much memory remembering every hash ever computed",
        "native-backend blank-node skolemization",
        "never seen that URI still means the same thing by it as one that has.",
        "never written, no StarLayerGraph's own _tt_nodes registry has it, so",
        "oldest-first eviction trades \"a very old, likely-no-longer-relevant ground",
        "proper TripleTerm instead of leaking the raw internal URIRef to the caller.",
        "registered TT_HASH_FN SPARQL function (starlayergraph.query.custom_functions)",
        "restore_select_bindings() below.",
        "the spot and never needs to have been written to any graph. Since it was",
        "triple-term content-addressed URIs",
        "value might need re-computing/re-remembering via TT_HASH_FN if looked up",
        "whenever it computes a hash for a fully-ground TRIPLE()/<<( )>> value used" ;
    slkg:contains <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding._canonicalize_numeric_literal>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding._reencode_tt>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding.canonicalize_query_result_value>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding.decode_dirlang_datatype>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding.encode_dirlang_datatype>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding.inject_missing_tt_encoding>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding.lookup_tt_hash>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding.remember_tt_hash>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding.restore_select_bindings>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding.term_key>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding.tt_hash> ;
    slkg:defines <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding._canonicalize_numeric_literal>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding._reencode_tt>,
        <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/kg/resource/function/starlayergraph.model.encoding.canonicalize_query_result_value>,
